<main id="landing-main">
  <section class="lp-hero lp-wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <img class="lp-hero-icon" src="./icon-192.png" width="80" height="80" alt="" />
    <p class="lp-eyebrow">INVENTORY MANAGEMENT, BY PUTER</p>
    <h1 id="hero-title">Stock in sight.<span>Work in hand.</span></h1>
    <p class="lp-lead">Know what you have, where it is, and what to reorder.<br class="lp-desktop-break" /> Products, suppliers, and daily stock changes in one clear workspace.</p>
    <div class="lp-actions"><button class="lp-button" data-sign-in disabled>Sign in <span data-icon="chevR" aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><a class="lp-text-link" href="/docs/getting-started/">Take a quick tour <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    <p class="lp-hero-note">Free to use <span>·</span> No ads <span>·</span> Your own Puter account</p>
    <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to sign in. Documentation and guides are available without it.</p></noscript>
    <figure class="lp-preview"><picture><source media="(max-width: 600px)" srcset="/screenshots/overview-mobile.png" /><img class="lp-hero-screenshot" src="/screenshots/overview-hero.webp" width="1312" height="847" fetchpriority="high" alt="Inventory overview showing stock value, low-stock alerts, replenishment needs, and recent activity." /></picture><figcaption>A working view of your stock. Shown with illustrative sample data.</figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <div class="lp-capabilities lp-wrap"><span>For shops, stockrooms, studios, and workshops</span><div><span>Stock by location</span><span>Barcode scanning</span><span>Supplier orders</span><span>CSV import &amp; export</span></div></div>
  <section class="lp-section lp-wrap" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
    <div class="lp-section-heading"><p class="lp-eyebrow">FROM THE FIRST RECEIPT TO THE NEXT REORDER</p><h2 id="features-title">Give every item a place.<br />Keep every change in view.</h2><p>Start with a few products. Keep the details connected as your stockroom grows.</p></div>
    <div class="lp-feature-grid">
      <article class="lp-feature lp-feature-wide"><div><span class="lp-feature-icon" data-icon="pin" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>Look beyond the total.</h3><p>See quantities and shelf codes at each location. Set local minimums and find stock you can move before buying more.</p><a class="lp-feature-tag" href="/docs/locations-and-replenishment/">Locations &amp; replenishment →</a></div><img class="lp-feature-shot" src="/screenshots/location-card.png" width="392" height="420" loading="lazy" alt="64 units across Warehouse, Studio, and Storefront; Storefront is six units below its minimum." /></article>
      <article class="lp-feature"><span class="lp-feature-icon" data-icon="cart" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>Know what to order next.</h3><p>Review low-stock alerts, days of cover, and suggested quantities. Compare supplier sources, prepare order sheets, and receive deliveries.</p><a class="lp-feature-tag" href="/docs/reordering-stock/">Reordering stock →</a><img class="lp-feature-shot" src="/screenshots/reorder-card.png" width="348" height="432" loading="lazy" alt="A supplier reorder sheet for a USB-C Hub and USB-C Cable, with editable quantities." /></article>
      <article class="lp-feature"><span class="lp-feature-icon" data-icon="chart" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>See what your stock is doing.</h3><p>Follow stock value, top movers, and slow-moving products. Review recorded revenue, cost of goods, and gross profit together.</p><a class="lp-feature-tag" href="/docs/reports-and-history/">Reports &amp; history →</a><img class="lp-feature-shot" src="/screenshots/sales-grid.png" width="388" height="251" loading="lazy" alt="Sample sales report with revenue, cost of goods, gross profit, and realized margin." /></article>
      <article class="lp-feature"><span class="lp-feature-icon" data-icon="barcode" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>Scan through the day's work.</h3><p>Gather sales, deliveries, or job materials in one take-out basket. Choose the location and reason, review the lines, and record the batch together.</p><a class="lp-feature-tag" href="/docs/scanning-and-take-out/">Scanning &amp; take out →</a></article>
      <article class="lp-feature"><span class="lp-feature-icon" data-icon="clipboard" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>Make every count count.</h3><p>Count by location, follow shelf codes around the room, and review differences before committing. Keep the stocktake report for your next review.</p><a class="lp-feature-tag" href="/docs/stocktakes/">Running a stocktake →</a></article>
      <article class="lp-feature"><span class="lp-feature-icon" data-icon="package" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>Room for the details.</h3><p>Track sizes and colours as variants, build kits from components, receive by the pack, and keep expiry dates in view.</p><a class="lp-feature-tag" href="/docs/variants-and-kits/">Variants &amp; kits →</a></article>
      <article class="lp-feature"><span class="lp-feature-icon" data-icon="fileUp" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>Bring your spreadsheet.</h3><p>Map CSV columns and review matches by SKU before importing. Export your products or download a full backup when you need your records.</p><a class="lp-feature-tag" href="/docs/importing-products/">Importing products →</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="lp-data" id="your-data" aria-labelledby="data-title"><div class="lp-data-inner lp-wrap"><div><p class="lp-eyebrow">YOUR STOCK. YOUR CLOUD.</p><h2 id="data-title">The records are yours.<br /><span>Keep them that way.</span></h2><p>Your inventory lives in your Puter account. Sign in to reach it on another device, and keep a downloadable backup of your records.</p><a href="/docs/backups-and-offline/">How storage and backups work →</a></div><div class="lp-data-points"><article><span data-icon="cloud" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><h3>Stored in your account</h3><p>Products, locations, suppliers, and activity use your Puter cloud storage.</p></div></article><article><span data-icon="wifiOff" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><h3>Keep working through a connection drop</h3><p>After an online visit, the app can use its local mirror and queue changes to sync when you reconnect.</p></div></article><article><span data-icon="download" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><h3>A copy you can keep</h3><p>Export products as CSV or download a JSON backup, including history and settings.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="lp-section lp-start lp-wrap" aria-labelledby="start-title"><div class="lp-section-heading"><p class="lp-eyebrow">A SMALL START IS A GOOD START</p><h2 id="start-title">From a list of products to a working inventory.</h2></div><div class="lp-steps"><article><span>01 / SIGN IN</span><h3>Make yourself at home.</h3><p>Continue with Puter, choose your currency, or explore the sample inventory first.</p></article><article><span>02 / SET UP</span><h3>Give stock a starting point.</h3><p>Add your locations and products, or <a href="/docs/importing-products/">import a CSV</a>. Check opening quantities and purchase costs.</p></article><article><span>03 / KEEP IT MOVING</span><h3>Record the everyday changes.</h3><p>Receive a delivery, take out stock, or move it between locations. Your overview and activity log follow along.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="lp-section lp-wrap" aria-labelledby="learn-title"><div class="lp-section-heading"><p class="lp-eyebrow">A LITTLE HELP, WHEN YOU NEED IT</p><h2 id="learn-title">Learn the tools.<br />Understand the numbers.</h2></div><div class="lp-resource-links"><article><h3>Documentation</h3><p>Step-by-step help for setting up products, receiving deliveries, counting stock, and keeping backups.</p><a class="lp-text-link" href="/docs/">Browse the docs →</a></article><article><h3>Practical guides</h3><p>Worked examples of reorder points, stock transfers, count differences, and inventory value.</p><a class="lp-text-link" href="/guides/">Explore the guides →</a></article></div></section>
  <section class="lp-section lp-faq lp-wrap" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div class="lp-section-heading"><p class="lp-eyebrow">GOOD QUESTIONS</p><h2 id="faq-title">Before you start.</h2></div><div class="lp-faq-list">
    <details><summary>Is Inventory free to use?</summary><p>Yes. Inventory is free to use and has no ads. A Puter account is required to save and sync your inventory.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I try it with sample data?</summary><p>Yes. Sign in and choose “Explore with sample data” in the welcome screen. The sample banner lets you clear that dataset when you are ready to start your own inventory.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I bring an existing spreadsheet?</summary><p>Export it as CSV, then review the column mapping and SKU matches in Inventory. You can update products, add to stock, or skip matches. See <a href="/docs/importing-products/">the import walkthrough</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I track more than one location?</summary><p>Yes. Each product can hold stock, a shelf code, and a minimum at each location. Transfers move units between places without changing the total quantity.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does it work with a barcode scanner?</summary><p>Use a compatible USB or Bluetooth scanner that types a barcode, enter codes yourself, or try the camera scanner where supported. Camera scanning requires browser support and camera permission.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I keep working offline?</summary><p>After loading the app online, its cached app shell and local mirror support connection drops. Changes queue on this device until you reconnect. A first visit or a new sign-in still needs a connection. Check the sync status before switching devices.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do I take my data with me?</summary><p>Settings includes product CSV export and a full JSON backup. Use the backup to restore records, including history and settings. Restoring replaces the current dataset; <a href="/docs/backups-and-offline/">review the backup workflow</a> first.</p></details>
  </div></section>
  <section class="lp-final lp-wrap" aria-labelledby="final-title"><img src="./icon-192.png" width="56" height="56" alt="" /><h2 id="final-title">Less guesswork.<br /><span>More stock in sight.</span></h2><p>Start with your first product, or explore a sample inventory.</p><button class="lp-button" data-sign-in disabled>Open Inventory <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><small>Free to use · Powered by Puter</small></section>
</main>
